      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": "\",\"variant\":\"heading\"},\"children\":[]}}\n{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/elements/exec-summary\",\"value\":{\"type\":\"TextBlock\",\"props\":{\"content\":\"Churn MRR is stat"
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": "istically heterogeneous across plans — both in absolute dollars and per-customer rate — pointing to a genuine plan"
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": "-tier retention problem rather than a scale artifact (Step 1). The $result:step_1_highest_churn_rate_plan"
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": " plan carries the highest pooled churn rate per customer at $result:step_1_highest_churn_rate_per_customer_value USD ("
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": "Step 1). Critically, expansion MRR and churn MRR move together with an overall correlation of $"
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": "result:step_2_overall_pearson_r, and this relationship holds within each plan tier,"
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": " indicating churn is structurally coupled to expansion — high-growth months simultaneously produce high churn,"
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": " consistent with a cohort-quality or onboarding problem rather than isolated retention failures ("
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": "Step 2). The churn-to-expansion ratio varies significantly across plans ($result:step_2_ratio_heterogeneity_test, p=$"
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": "result:step_2_ratio_heterogeneity_p), confirming the coupling intensity differs by segment (Step 2).\",\"variant\":\"insight\"},\"children\":[]}}"
    },
