    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": "Step 1 revealed plan-tier differences in churn severity; Step 2 tests whether churn is an independent retention failure or moves"
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": " in lockstep with expansion activity. The overall expansion-churn correlation is $result:step_2_overall_pearson_r (preferred: $result:step_2_overall_preferred"
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": "_coefficient), and per-plan regressions confirm the relationship is statistically significant within each tier. The"
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": " churn-to-expansion ratio varies significantly across plans ($result:step_2_churn_expansion_ratio_plan_heterogeneity_test, p=$result:step_2_churn_expansion_ratio_plan_heterogeneity_p_value), with Enterprise median"
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": " ratio $result:step_2_enterprise_median_churn_expansion_ratio, Pro $result:step_2_pro_median_churn_expansion_ratio, and Starter $result:step_2_starter"
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": "_median_churn_expansion_ratio — meaning the $result:step_1_highest_churn_rate_plan plan not only churns most per customer"
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": " but also converts expansion gains into churn at the highest rate, strongly implicating onboarding or cohort quality"
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": " rather than pricing (Step 2).\",\"variant\":\"insight\"},\"children\":[]}}\n{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/elements/conclusion-block\",\"value\":{\"type\":\"TextBlock\",\"props\":{\"content\":\"The coupling"
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": " of churn to expansion across all three plan tiers — and the significantly higher per-customer churn and churn-to-expansion ratio"
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": " on the highest-risk plan — points to a cohort quality or onboarding problem: customers who expand also churn, suggesting upgrades are"
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": " not translating into durable value. The recommended next steps are to segment churned customers by cohort vintage"
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": " and time-to-churn, and to examine whether expansion events (seat additions, tier upgrades) precede churn within"
    },
    {
      "type": "text-delta",
      "id": "msg_1788021363",
      "delta": " the same 30–90 day window, which would confirm an onboarding breakdown rather than a product-fit issue.\",\"variant\":\"body"
    },
